course: dictionary
lesson: 9308
title: Spectacled and words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Spectacled means wearing glasses. Spectacles is an old word for glasses, so a spectacled person has glasses on their face.
explain: In animal names, spectacled means having rings or marks around the eyes that look like glasses. «The spectacled bear of the Andes, with pale rings around its eyes, is the only bear in South America.» The pale rings are the clue: they look like glasses, so the name fits.
explain: When you meet a new word, ask what would fit here, then try your meaning in the sentence. «A spectacled old man» sits in a story, and the words around it tell you he wears glasses.
explain: Spectacled is a slightly old-fashioned, bookish word, so you will often meet it in stories and science books. If the context is not enough, check a dictionary.
fact: Spectacled means wearing glasses.
fact: In animal names, spectacled means having rings or marks around the eyes that look like glasses.
fact: «Spectacled bear» and «spectacled owl» are animal names that use this meaning.
fact: Spectacled is a slightly old-fashioned, bookish word.
fact: The spectacled bear lives in the Andes in South America, climbs trees, and eats mostly plants and fruit.
exercise: «The spectacled bear of the Andes, with pale rings around its eyes, is the only bear in South America.» What are the rings around its eyes like? | Like a crown | *Like glasses | Like a bird's wings | Like paint on a fence
exercise: «A spectacled old man sat by the window.» What does spectacled tell you about him? | He is always singing | He lives in a tree | He has lost his shoes | *He wears glasses
exercise: Spectacled is an old-fashioned, bookish word. Where would you be most likely to find it? | *A story or a science book about animals | A shopping list | A text message to a friend | A football scoreboard
test: «The eight bears are the brown bear, American black bear, polar bear, Asiatic black bear, sun bear, sloth bear, spectacled bear and giant panda.» Which of these is NOT one of the eight bears? | Sloth bear | Sun bear | Polar bear | *Koala
test: In «spectacled owl», what does spectacled tell you about the owl? | It can fly | *It has marks around its eyes that look like glasses | It is very big | It lives in a city
exam: «The spectacled old man read the newspaper.» What does spectacled mean here? | *Wearing glasses | Hiding behind a tree | Very tired | Running fast
